WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Matthew, Chapter Twenty-Six.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:13.867
And it came to pass, when Jesus had finished all these sayings, he said unto his disciples, Ye know that after two days is the feast of the passover, and the Son of man is betrayed to be crucified.

3
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:24.933
Then assembled together the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders of the people, unto the palace of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas, And consulted that they might take Jesus by subtilty, and kill him.

4
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:29.733
But they said, Not on the feast day, lest there be an uproar among the people.

5
00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:41.867
Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper, There came unto him a woman having an alabaster box of very precious ointment, and poured it on his head, as he sat at meat.

6
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:48.000
But when his disciples saw it, they had indignation, saying, To what purpose is this waste?

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.533
For this ointment might have been sold for much, and given to the poor.

8
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:56.800
When Jesus understood it, he said unto them, Why trouble ye the woman?

9
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.333
for she hath wrought a good work upon me.

10
00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:03.600
For ye have the poor always with you; but me ye have not always.

11
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.067
For in that she hath poured this ointment on my body, she did it for my burial.

12
00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:17.733
Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world, there shall also this, that this woman hath done, be told for a memorial of her.

13
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:28.000
Then one of the twelve, called Judas Iscariot, went unto the chief priests, And said unto them, What will ye give me, and I will deliver him unto you?

14
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.933
And they covenanted with him for thirty pieces of silver.

15
00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:34.533
And from that time he sought opportunity to betray him.

16
00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:43.867
Now the first day of the feast of unleavened bread the disciples came to Jesus, saying unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the passover?

17
00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:53.733
And he said, Go into the city to such a man, and say unto him, The Master saith, My time is at hand; I will keep the passover at thy house with my disciples.

18
00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:58.400
And the disciples did as Jesus had appointed them; and they made ready the passover.

19
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.267
Now when the even was come, he sat down with the twelve.

20
00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:08.133
And as they did eat, he said, Verily I say unto you, that one of you shall betray me.

21
00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:14.267
And they were exceeding sorrowful, and began every one of them to say unto him, Lord, is it I?

22
00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:20.133
And he answered and said, He that dippeth his hand with me in the dish, the same shall betray me.

23
00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:27.333
The Son of man goeth as it is written of him: but woe unto that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed!

24
00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:30.267
it had been good for that man if he had not been born.

25
00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:36.000
Then Judas, which betrayed him, answered and said, Master, is it I?

26
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.800
He said unto him, Thou hast said.

27
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:48.933
And as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.

28
00:02:48.933 --> 00:02:58.533
And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and gave it to them, saying, Drink ye all of it; For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.

29
00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:06.533
But I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father's kingdom.

30
00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:10.267
And when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.

31
00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:20.400
Then saith Jesus unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.

32
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.267
But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.

33
00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:30.933
Peter answered and said unto him, Though all men shall be offended because of thee, yet will I never be offended.

34
00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:37.867
Jesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.

35
00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:43.067
Peter said unto him, Though I should die with thee, yet will I not deny thee.

36
00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:46.000
Likewise also said all the disciples.

37
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:54.533
Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the disciples, Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder.

38
00:03:54.533 --> 00:04:00.533
And he took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and very heavy.

39
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:07.867
Then saith he unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death: tarry ye here, and watch with me.

40
00:04:07.867 --> 00:04:18.667
And he went a little further, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless not as I will, but as thou wilt.

41
00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:26.400
And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, and saith unto Peter, What, could ye not watch with me one hour?

42
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:32.667
Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.

43
00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:42.667
He went away again the second time, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if this cup may not pass away from me, except I drink it, thy will be done.

44
00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:46.667
And he came and found them asleep again: for their eyes were heavy.

45
00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:52.400
And he left them, and went away again, and prayed the third time, saying the same words.

46
00:04:52.400 --> 00:05:04.533
Then cometh he to his disciples, and saith unto them, Sleep on now, and take your rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.

47
00:05:04.533 --> 00:05:08.800
Rise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that doth betray me.

48
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:18.133
And while he yet spake, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and elders of the people.

49
00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:26.667
Now he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he: hold him fast.

50
00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:31.200
And forthwith he came to Jesus, and said, Hail, master; and kissed him.

51
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.333
And Jesus said unto him, Friend, wherefore art thou come?

52
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:39.200
Then came they, and laid hands on Jesus, and took him.

53
00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:47.333
And, behold, one of them which were with Jesus stretched out his hand, and drew his sword, and struck a servant of the high priest's, and smote off his ear.

54
00:05:47.333 --> 00:05:55.200
Then said Jesus unto him, Put up again thy sword into his place: for all they that take the sword shall perish with the sword.

55
00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:01.600
Thinkest thou that I cannot now pray to my Father, and he shall presently give me more than twelve legions of angels?

56
00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.267
But how then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?

57
00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:14.133
In that same hour said Jesus to the multitudes, Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staves for to take me?

58
00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:18.667
I sat daily with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me.

59
00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:22.800
But all this was done, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled.

60
00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.000
Then all the disciples forsook him, and fled.

61
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:32.400
And they that had laid hold on Jesus led him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled.

62
00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:39.733
But Peter followed him afar off unto the high priest's palace, and went in, and sat with the servants, to see the end.

63
00:06:39.733 --> 00:06:52.133
Now the chief priests, and elders, and all the council, sought false witness against Jesus, to put him to death; But found none: yea, though many false witnesses came, yet found they none.

64
00:06:52.133 --> 00:07:01.733
At the last came two false witnesses, And said, This fellow said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.

65
00:07:01.733 --> 00:07:05.867
And the high priest arose, and said unto him, Answerest thou nothing?

66
00:07:05.867 --> 00:07:08.933
what is it which these witness against thee?

67
00:07:08.933 --> 00:07:10.933
But Jesus held his peace.

68
00:07:10.933 --> 00:07:18.933
And the high priest answered and said unto him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be the Christ, the Son of God.

69
00:07:18.933 --> 00:07:31.333
Jesus saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.

70
00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:37.600
Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further need have we of witnesses?

71
00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:43.867
behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.

72
00:07:43.867 --> 00:07:45.067
What think ye?

73
00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:48.000
They answered and said, He is guilty of death.

74
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:57.733
Then did they spit in his face, and buffeted him; and others smote him with the palms of their hands, Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee?

75
00:07:57.733 --> 00:08:06.267
Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of Galilee.

76
00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:10.400
But he denied before them all, saying, I know not what thou sayest.

77
00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:18.800
And when he was gone out into the porch, another maid saw him, and said unto them that were there, This fellow was also with Jesus of Nazareth.

78
00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:22.267
And again he denied with an oath, I do not know the man.

79
00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:30.800
And after a while came unto him they that stood by, and said to Peter, Surely thou also art one of them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.

80
00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:35.867
Then began he to curse and to swear, saying, I know not the man.

81
00:08:35.867 --> 00:08:37.467
And immediately the cock crew.

82
00:08:37.467 --> 00:08:43.467
And Peter remembered the word of Jesus, which said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.

83
00:08:43.467 --> 00:08:45.600
And he went out, and wept bitterly.

